    "q-175552": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175552",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the set of positive integers:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd\n\n- $Q(x):$ $12$ is divisible by $x$",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ represents the *intersection* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∧Q}={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$ \n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of all positive odd integers, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{1,3,5,7,9,11,13…\\}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=\\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∧Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,5,7,9,11,13…\\}\\cap \\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,3\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-175552-a",
